WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.984
- It feels incredible to
be a part of the list.

00:00:01.984 --> 00:00:04.851
If you had told me a couple
of years ago that this was

00:00:04.851 --> 00:00:08.336
gonna happen, I would've told
you that you have to be lying.

00:00:08.336 --> 00:00:10.060
It's totally unbelievable.

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:11.548
(dramatic music)

00:00:11.548 --> 00:00:14.089
I'm Arantxa Unda, and
I'm the CEO of Sigesa.

00:00:14.089 --> 00:00:18.824
It's the company that we do
coding and analytics tools

00:00:18.824 --> 00:00:23.039
for management decision
support in health care.

00:00:23.039 --> 00:00:24.950
I have a bit of a different story

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:26.344
to some other entrepreneurs.

00:00:26.344 --> 00:00:29.114
I actually started my
career working in finance.

00:00:29.114 --> 00:00:31.429
I was not very convinced by that.

00:00:31.429 --> 00:00:34.094
And my father, together
with some other partners,

00:00:34.094 --> 00:00:38.748
he upstarted a company
that did health care IT.

00:00:38.748 --> 00:00:41.742
And I decided to give it a
try, and work for the company,

00:00:41.742 --> 00:00:44.467
and became really passionate
about health care,

00:00:44.467 --> 00:00:47.979
and a firm believer of the
value of universal care

00:00:47.979 --> 00:00:49.865
and public health care systems.

00:00:49.865 --> 00:00:53.029
So I decided to go to the
US, pursue an MBA in Harvard

00:00:53.029 --> 00:00:54.651
to get more managerial skills.

00:00:54.651 --> 00:00:58.909
And on my way back to Spain
I raised some financing,

00:00:58.909 --> 00:01:01.892
bought out the company, and
I've transformed the company

00:01:01.892 --> 00:01:04.432
and I'm looking to expand it.

00:01:04.432 --> 00:01:06.849
It's very different to just
like work at the company

00:01:06.849 --> 00:01:11.037
to just actually own the
company and have the challenge

00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:15.128
to transform a company looking
to, trying to transform

00:01:15.128 --> 00:01:17.038
an industry as a whole.

00:01:17.038 --> 00:01:19.770
So I think it's knowing
that what you're doing is,

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:22.156
actually has an impact,
that you're working

00:01:22.156 --> 00:01:24.320
to transform an industry.

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:27.322
And it's something that you
firmly believe in, like I do.

00:01:27.322 --> 00:01:29.561
For me, it's public health care systems.

00:01:29.561 --> 00:01:31.750
And I think that some days
when you have a hard day

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:34.399
and you have to wake
up and just go to work,

00:01:34.399 --> 00:01:37.017
you're realizing you're
doing something that really

00:01:37.017 --> 00:01:39.878
adds value, and that keeps you going.

00:01:39.878 --> 00:01:42.762
So I think it's find something
that you're passionate about.

00:01:42.762 --> 00:01:46.261
Also be very persistent in your work.

00:01:46.261 --> 00:01:48.265
And also for someone
like me, if you've worked

00:01:48.265 --> 00:01:50.462
in something like finance
or consulting before,

00:01:50.462 --> 00:01:53.985
to understand that working in a startup or

00:01:53.985 --> 00:01:56.758
at a small company that's
growing, it's very different.

00:01:56.758 --> 00:02:00.011
That you have to make sometimes
decisions pretty fast,

00:02:00.011 --> 00:02:03.244
and you can't have all the
analysis you want with you,

00:02:03.244 --> 00:02:06.260
'cause otherwise you'll get
stuck in paralysis by analysis.

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:10.783
You need to trust yourself,
and you also need to be,

00:02:10.783 --> 00:02:13.134
just trust your gut.

00:02:13.134 --> 00:02:15.169
So for us the next step is scaling.

00:02:15.169 --> 00:02:18.301
We're building new
products for our portfolio,

00:02:18.301 --> 00:02:21.345
and we're looking to scale
in different countries, too.

00:02:21.345 --> 00:02:24.095
(dramatic music)

